Close the day at midnight and on the first wake of a new day; read the current
count before the first event

The date change was handled only inside the next interval recording, so the
live total (sensor minus offset) carried the old day into the new one for up
to ten minutes, and a phone asleep across midnight rolled over only at its
first record after waking. A single-shot timer to 00:00:01 forces a recording
(the rollover) and re-arms; timeUpdate(), which runs on every display-on,
records at once when the date has changed.

A new sensorfw session sees no value until the next step event; a loader that
had just started showed the last log record instead of the live count. Until
the first event steps() reads the sensor's D-Bus property, which carries the
current value for every session.

